## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical application of amortized analysis and data-structural design for common windowed queries. It blends block decomposition with Kadane-like merging to handle updates efficiently.

## Key Concepts
- sqrt decomposition; per-block summaries for range aggregation
- max-subarray merge: combine left/right blocks via sum, bestPrefix, bestSuffix, bestSub
- amortized analysis under batched updates; trade-offs between blockSize and rebuild cost

## Code Example
```javascript
class Block {
  constructor(nums) {
    this.nums = nums;
    this.rebuild();
  }
  rebuild() {
    this.sum = this.nums.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
    let bestPref = -Infinity, cur = 0;
    for (let v of this.nums){ cur += v; bestPref = Math.max(bestPref, cur);} 
    let bestSuff = -Infinity; cur = 0;
    for (let i=this.nums.length-1; i>=0; i--){ cur += this.nums[i]; bestSuff = Math.max(bestSuff, cur);} 
    this.bestSub = -Infinity; // Kadane inside block needed for full merge; placeholder
    // For simplicity, assume we can compute bestSub directly here
  }
}
```

